  "interpretation": [
    "Earlier completed-target scanout remains 140 ms for insertion; the previous readiness gate did not hide an earlier complete update in these samples.",
    "The first changed logical cell appears around 60 ms. This is not a claim that the typed glyph is already visible.",
    "Two sequential public console requests consume about 55 ms elapsed. Their transfer/wait portions consume about 52 ms.",
    "Presenter spans total about 8 ms elapsed. Model-copy spans total about 0.53 ms. Request elapsed time cannot be equated with glyph drawing cost.",
    "An insertion uses 74 native cell calls and 75 guest/bridge returns. Their call counts still justify a bounded cell path improvement.",
    "Inclusive routine intervals include preemption, can overlap across Tasks, and must not be summed as exclusive CPU costs.",
    "The last interval includes read rearming and final scanout; this trace does not isolate that interval further."
  ],
